{"4410790": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "The Fibrous - Operation Reclaim", "steam_appid": 4410790, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A Third-Person (Over-the-shoulder) shooter/adventure game covering the story of a ex-marine who had a mission go sour and gave up the career. UNTIL - A meteor hits earth a few years later and fibrous-skinned aliens emerge from within and begin taking over Earth! Finick (The Ex-marine) is recruited by what's left of the military to help steal DNA-samples from the alien, coined - The Fibrous, due to their fiber-like appearance. Will you be able to help learn their origins, and weaknesses, and take back Earth? or let another mission go sour and lose your planet?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Developer's Timeline:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game will originally release with ONLY the multi-player (Online singleplayer or multiplayer) functionality built. Therefore the price will be lowered accordingly. I am a single (fully employed) adult with children so this is really a passion project that will be worked on in my free-time and depending on the community it builds and demand for more? (I have high hopes I know) I have hopes on building a full-fledged single-player campaign rich with the actual lore of the aliens and our ex-marine, Finick. If this is done and the campaign is added, the price of the game will be increased to match the update. I do not plan to ever add in-game purchases or skins or anything of the sort, I want the game to be purchased and fully in-game unlockable items/story/lore.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Dev Notes:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >While I've spent many a day trying to optimize every file in the game and doing everything I know how to to keep the file sizes small the game is still pretty graphically intensive. Of course you have options to reduce the quality to try and increase frame rate and for those with compatible-graphics cards there is the option for DLSS.</p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A Third-Person (Over-the-shoulder) shooter/adventure game covering the story of a ex-marine who had a mission go sour and gave up the career. UNTIL - A meteor hits earth a few years later and fibrous-skinned aliens emerge from within and begin taking over Earth! Finick (The Ex-marine) is recruited by what's left of the military to help steal DNA-samples from the alien, coined - The Fibrous, due to their fiber-like appearance. Will you be able to help learn their origins, and weaknesses, and take back Earth? or let another mission go sour and lose your planet?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Developer's Timeline:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game will originally release with ONLY the multi-player (Online singleplayer or multiplayer) functionality built. Therefore the price will be lowered accordingly. I am a single (fully employed) adult with children so this is really a passion project that will be worked on in my free-time and depending on the community it builds and demand for more? (I have high hopes I know) I have hopes on building a full-fledged single-player campaign rich with the actual lore of the aliens and our ex-marine, Finick. If this is done and the campaign is added, the price of the game will be increased to match the update. I do not plan to ever add in-game purchases or skins or anything of the sort, I want the game to be purchased and fully in-game unlockable items/story/lore.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Dev Notes:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >While I've spent many a day trying to optimize every file in the game and doing everything I know how to to keep the file sizes small the game is still pretty graphically intensive. Of course you have options to reduce the quality to try and increase frame rate and for those with compatible-graphics cards there is the option for DLSS.</p>", "short_description": "The Fibrous - Sci-Fi Online or Single-Player TPS (Over-The-Shoulder) covering the story of an ex-marine recruited by what's left of the military to help take back Earth after a meteor crash-lands into Earth and aliens with fiber-like skin emerge, thinking they can take this planet for their own.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4410790/385ec89e5492e26c3afb78bc7503206c1ede7835/header.jpg?t=1782736063", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4410790/a7271bfc7488811820b269f47d972fbecb3e9e50/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1782736063", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4410790/a7271bfc7488811820b269f47d972fbecb3e9e50/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1782736063", "website": null, "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Ryzen 5 9600X (6-Core / 12-Thread) OR Core Ultra 5 250K Plus (18-Core)<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 16 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> Geforce Dedicated Graphics 30 Series (Tested on 2 separate versions)<br></li><li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 11<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 16 GB available space</li></ul>"}, "mac_requirements": [], "linux_requirements": [], "developers": ["Matthew Klinekole"], "publishers": ["Matthew Klinekole"], "price_overview": {"currency": "USD", "initial": 799, "final": 799, "discount_percent": 0, "initial_formatted": "", "final_formatted": "$7.99"}, "packages": [1540380], "package_groups": [{"name": "default", "title": "Buy The Fibrous - Operation Reclaim", "description": "", "selection_text": "Select a purchase option", "save_text": "", "display_type": 0, "is_recurring_subscrip